WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.376
Chapter six: reviewing a paper. Formal reviews are the heart of Scholium.

00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:10.171
They are structured and signed, they appear next to the paper, and they decide its status.

00:00:10.171 --> 00:00:13.084
This chapter is for reviewers, and for authors.

00:00:13.084 --> 00:00:21.045
A formal review is different from discussion, which is open to any member, and from the AI pre-review, which only advises.

00:00:21.045 --> 00:00:24.843
You need tier three, Reviewer, which the node operator grants.

00:00:24.843 --> 00:00:28.273
You cannot review a paper if you are one of its authors.

00:00:28.273 --> 00:00:33.819
You write one review per paper, across all its versions, and you need no invitation.

00:00:33.819 --> 00:00:37.627
An author or a moderator can invite a tier three reviewer.

00:00:37.627 --> 00:00:40.910
The invitation appears under Needs your attention.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:46.037
In this release it is only a pointer, with nothing to accept or decline.

00:00:46.037 --> 00:00:50.930
Here is the flow. Open the form, pass the conflict check, and fill the rubric.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:54.505
Commit the review, and it stays sealed. Later, reveal it.

00:00:54.505 --> 00:00:59.045
The authors reply, and after a new version you update your review.

00:00:59.045 --> 00:01:03.284
To start, open the Reviews tab of the paper and choose Review this paper.

00:01:03.284 --> 00:01:06.123
The review form shows the paper beside it.

00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:11.331
The form runs three conflict checks, and marks each one pass, fail or unknown.

00:01:11.331 --> 00:01:13.668
First: not an author of this paper.

00:01:13.668 --> 00:01:17.941
Second: no co-authorship with an author in the last three years.

00:01:17.941 --> 00:01:20.411
Third: a different institution.

00:01:20.411 --> 00:01:22.414
Only the first check blocks you.

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:29.048
The other two are advisory: if one fails, decide whether you can review fairly, and decline if you cannot.

00:01:29.048 --> 00:01:33.141
Without a saved affiliation, the form asks you to save one.

00:01:33.141 --> 00:01:37.801
By default, you review anonymously, as Reviewer A, Reviewer B, and so on.

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:41.840
Your letter for the paper stays the same across versions.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.318
Scholium does not store your identity in readable form.

00:01:45.318 --> 00:01:50.187
At commit, it encrypts your identity with the key of the integrity committee.

00:01:50.187 --> 00:01:52.800
Only a misconduct case can open it.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:56.443
In this release, the escrow uses a single committee key.

00:01:56.443 --> 00:02:00.738
A scheme that needs several committee members to agree is planned.

00:02:00.738 --> 00:02:04.976
Nobody can open an identity through the website or the API.

00:02:04.976 --> 00:02:08.266
For public credit, choose Sign with my name instead.

00:02:08.266 --> 00:02:16.448
When you come back to a signed review, the form opens in the signed state on any device, and offers Stay anonymous instead.

00:02:16.448 --> 00:02:22.524
After the reveal, a signed review keeps its letter, and shows Signed by, with a link to your profile.

00:02:22.524 --> 00:02:26.533
It also appears under Signed reviews on your public profile.

00:02:26.533 --> 00:02:28.001
Next, fill the rubric.

00:02:28.001 --> 00:02:33.937
Score each of six dimensions from one to five, and write a justification for every score.

00:02:33.937 --> 00:02:36.939
Scholium rejects a review without them.

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:45.360
The six dimensions are soundness of method, evidence for claims, reproducibility, novelty, clarity, and limitations and ethics.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.168
Set your confidence: low, medium or high.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:51.866
Then choose a recommendation, which drives the status.

00:02:51.866 --> 00:02:55.565
Sound as is and Minor revisions count toward Reviewed.

00:02:55.565 --> 00:02:58.578
Major concerns keeps the paper Under review.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.718
Fundamentally flawed makes it Contested.

00:03:01.718 --> 00:03:04.989
You can add an optional written report in Markdown.

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:07.554
If you used AI assistance, tick the box.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:12.059
After the reveal, your review then shows AI assistance declared.

00:03:12.059 --> 00:03:17.034
Then choose Commit review. This signs the review with a per-paper key and seals it.

00:03:17.034 --> 00:03:22.528
Nobody can read it yet: not the authors, not the other reviewers, and not the server.

00:03:22.528 --> 00:03:25.719
The seal stops reviewers from influencing each other.

00:03:25.719 --> 00:03:33.766
A review can be revealed when a second reviewer commits on the same version, or 21 days after the first commit on that version.

00:03:33.766 --> 00:03:37.542
The form shows where things stand: here, one review so far.

00:03:37.542 --> 00:03:41.846
This review can be revealed after one more, or on a set date.

00:03:41.846 --> 00:03:46.759
Save your review key. The reveal secret stays in the browser where you committed.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:51.552
Export it as a review key file, with a passphrase of at least eight characters.

00:03:51.552 --> 00:03:55.046
Without it, you cannot reveal from another browser.

00:03:55.046 --> 00:03:58.159
Scholium does not reveal reviews automatically.

00:03:58.159 --> 00:04:02.531
When the gate opens, go back to the form and choose Reveal review.

00:04:02.531 --> 00:04:08.032
Your rubric, recommendation and report then become public on the Reviews tab.

00:04:08.032 --> 00:04:13.168
Until then, the Reviews tab shows the review as sealed, and says when it can open.

00:04:13.168 --> 00:04:19.665
Authors can answer a review point by point: one reply per rubric dimension, plus a general reply.

00:04:19.665 --> 00:04:22.881
Replies appear under the review as Author reply.

00:04:22.881 --> 00:04:26.027
Only people on the author list can reply.

00:04:26.027 --> 00:04:30.427
When the authors publish a new version, choose Update for the new version.

00:04:30.427 --> 00:04:35.643
An update needs a complete rubric again. It can replace your earlier review once.

00:04:35.643 --> 00:04:39.107
An update publishes your scores and recommendation at once.

00:04:39.107 --> 00:04:43.851
Your written report follows when the reveal gate of the new version opens.

00:04:43.851 --> 00:04:49.701
A reviewer who did not write a review, and is not an author, can rate it once, from one to five.

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:54.088
You rate the review, not the paper, and ratings never change the status.

00:04:54.088 --> 00:04:56.987
Reviewer reputation is planned for later.

00:04:56.987 --> 00:04:59.350
How is the status of a paper decided?

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:04.908
Scholium uses only signed records and a fixed rule, so any server gets the same answer.

00:05:04.908 --> 00:05:08.502
It works down this list, and the first match wins.

00:05:08.502 --> 00:05:11.787
A reviewer's current review is their latest update.

00:05:11.787 --> 00:05:18.502
Discussion, helpful votes, review ratings, AI findings and withdrawal notices never change status.

00:05:18.502 --> 00:05:24.373
As an author, you can reply to each review, and publish a new version that answers the reviews.

00:05:24.373 --> 00:05:27.278
Reviewers can then update their recommendation.

00:05:27.278 --> 00:05:31.510
If necessary, you can issue a correction or retraction notice.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.806
In short: one review per paper, from tier three.

00:05:34.806 --> 00:05:41.193
Score six dimensions, commit a sealed review, and reveal it after a second review or 21 days.

00:05:41.193 --> 00:05:46.950
A fixed rule sets the status. Next, chapter seven: discussion and annotations.
